       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf the 6,400 mg/day dose is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
