       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen has no accepted clinical use. It's double the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is double the maximum single dose. The main risks are GI hemorrhage and acute kidney injury, and a patient with normal organ function wouldn't be protected from them. I can't enter it on the strength of the confirmation alone.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the limits.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the highest standard regimen. I can enter it now.\n- **Review with your attending or a clinical pharmacist.** If you think this patient needs an unusual dose, they can help confirm it. I can enter it once the plan is documented that way.\n- **Look at other options.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, adding acetaminophen or changing agents may work better than raising the ibuprofen dose.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it."
      }
